@startuml ftq_request
title Ready prediction -> FTQ admission -> fetch consumption
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 call or signal
  [N] New IBPU / bridge / helper connection
  [A] Model algorithm; illustrative private operation
endlegend

participant "o3::BAC" as BAC
participant Gem5BpuBridge as Bridge
participant IBPU as BPU
participant ResponseQueue as Q
participant "o3::CPU" as CPU
participant "o3::FTQ" as FTQ
participant "FTQ probes / optional FDP" as Probes
participant "o3::Fetch" as Fetch

note over BAC, FTQ
  Sources: bac.cc BAC::generateFetchTargets() (585),
  BAC::newFetchTarget() (554); ftq.cc insert() (186), popHead() (238).
  New mode substitutes bridge admission for legacy target generation.
end note

BAC -> Bridge : [N] service(now, credits)
ref over Bridge, BPU
  First tick IBPU and handle due control events (tick_path.puml).
  This diagram expands only the subsequent data-admission phase.
end ref
loop while insertion budget remains and recovery permits admission
    Bridge -> FTQ : [N] reuse isReady(tid), isLocked(tid), numFreeEntries(tid)
    FTQ --> Bridge : [E] validity, lock state and free physical entries
    alt invalid/locked/full, draining, or model has no hardware credits
        Bridge -> Bridge : [A] stop admission; leave pending result in IBPU
        note over BPU, FTQ
          isReady() alone is insufficient: Locked is not Invalid.
          No publication means no acceptFetchTarget() call.
          Do not shift readyCycle for a result that is already ready.
        end note
    else target may be admitted
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] canSupply(now)
        BPU -> Q : [N] peekReady(now)
        Q --> BPU : [N] valid head with readyCycle <= now, or none
        BPU --> Bridge : [N] ready?
        alt no ready target
            Bridge -> Bridge : [A] stop this admission loop
        else ready target exists
            Bridge -> BPU : [N] peekFetchTarget()
            BPU --> Bridge : [N] stable BpuFetchTargetPtr + dynamic key
            Bridge -> Bridge : [N] makeFT(payload)
            Bridge -> CPU : [N] reuse getAndIncrementFTSeq()
            CPU --> Bridge : [E] new FTSeqNum
            Bridge -> Bridge : [A] attach payload; map FTSeqNum to prediction key
            Bridge -> FTQ : [N] reuse insert(tid, ft)
            FTQ -> FTQ : [E] assert capacity; push_back(ft)
            FTQ -> Probes : [E] ppFTQInsert->notify(ft)
            opt FDP is configured
                Probes -> Probes : [N] enumerate actual FetchBlock ranges
                note right of Probes
                  Existing FDP reads one start/end interval.
                  Multi-block mode must not prefetch address gaps.
                end note
            end
            FTQ --> Bridge : [E] insert returns (void)
            Bridge -> BPU : [N] acceptFetchTarget(key, now)
            BPU -> Q : [N] accept(key)
            Bridge -> Bridge : [A] decrement per-cycle insert budget and credits
        end
    end
end

... CPU::tick invokes Fetch::tick after BAC::tick ...
Fetch -> FTQ : [E] isHeadReady(tid), readHead(tid)
FTQ --> Fetch : [E] FetchTargetPtr or unavailable
ref over Fetch, FTQ
  fetch_blocks_merge.puml / predecode_feedback.puml
  process ordered blocks; bind every observed instruction/CFI
end ref
alt target fully consumed and prediction audit permits removal
    Fetch -> FTQ : [E] popHead(tid), with new multi-block completion checks
    alt legacy bpuHistory is still attached
        FTQ -> FTQ : [E] mark Invalid; retain head; no remove notification
        FTQ --> Fetch : [E] false, no entry removed
        Fetch -> Fetch : [A] stop and request metadata repair
    else head has no legacy bpuHistory
        opt FTQ was Locked
            FTQ -> FTQ : [E] mark Invalid; set return value false
        end
        FTQ -> Probes : [E] ppFTQRemove->notify(ft)
        FTQ -> FTQ : [E] pop_front()
        FTQ --> Fetch : [E] true normally; false if Locked, despite removal
        Fetch -> BAC : [N] report key after confirming actual removal
        BAC -> Bridge : [N] forward target-consumed notification
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] onTargetConsumed(key), exactly once
        BPU -> BPU : [A] retain history until model release point
        opt pop returned false
            Fetch -> Fetch : [A] stop and request recovery of invalid FTQ
        end
    end
else unmatched prediction / boundary repair / incomplete target
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] retain target or enter predecode recovery; no false consumption
end

note over BPU, FTQ
  issueCycle, readyCycle and FTQ acceptedCycle are different timestamps.
  One FTQ slot holds one target group, possibly with several blocks.
  Model retention credits may outlive physical FTQ pop.
  New payloads keep legacy bpuHistory null; IBPU owns their ledger.
  A false popHead return alone does not describe ownership changes.
  Budget updates take effect at the chosen hardware phase;
  Fetch frees entries after BAC admission in the current CPU tick order.
end note
@enduml
